Description: Use the desktop's dark icons on a dark palette
 umplayer's icons are drawn for a light window: pale glossy bodies, bright
 colours and a shadow that only shows on white. On a dark palette, as minos has,
 they glare: the large pictures of the preferences, the list of its sections,
 the icons of every menu (the same actions fill the popup, the tray menu, the
 toolbars and the shortcuts table), and the buttons of the shortcuts editor and
 the playlist. When the window colour of the palette is dark, take the icon of
 the same meaning from the desktop's icon theme (on minos laga, drawn for black)
 at the size of the original; a light palette, or a theme without that icon,
 keeps umplayer's own. laga has no funnel, so the two menus of filters take its
 gear; umplayer's own logo (About UMPlayer) has no drawing there and stays.
Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/images.cpp b/src/images.cpp
