+// shadow that only shows on white. On a dark palette they glare; the desktop's icon theme has
+// icons of the same meaning drawn for it (on minos, laga). Names are tried in order: the
+// freedesktop name first where one means the same, then the name laga ships; a name the
+// theme lacks leaves umplayer's own icon. Qt does not enlarge a theme icon, so the first
+// names are ones laga has at least as large as the original.
+static QPixmap darkThemeIcon(const QString & name, const QSize & size) {
+	static const char * const map[][5] = {
